/*
SubmitQuote Submit a draft for approval

Price the quote in full (tax included) and route it. Below the approval threshold (first
invoice amount or largest discount) it becomes `approved` at once and can be sent. At or
above the threshold it becomes `pending_approval` and waits for a second person in the
console's approval queue. There is no API to approve or reject a quote, because the
two-person rule needs a person who is not the quote's owner.

A quote with no lines, or one that is not a draft, is `409 quote_refused`. When tax cannot
be calculated, the answer is the shared tax refusal (`422 tax_service_not_connected` or
`503 tax_calculation_unavailable`) or `409 seller_incomplete`.


 @param ctx context.Context - for authentication, logging, cancellation, deadlines, tracing, etc. Passed from http.Request or context.Background().
 @param number The quote number, unique within the token's environment, or the quote's public id (`quo_…`).
 @return ApiSubmitQuoteRequest
*/
